        "title": "Human Impacts: Overfishing, Runoff, Physical Damage, Tourism",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Coral reefs face simultaneous stressors operating at multiple scales — local (overfishing, runoff, physical damage) and global (warming, acidification). The local stressors compound the global ones: a reef with intact herbivore populations can recover from bleaching faster than a heavily fished reef. Management of local stressors is therefore one of the few levers available to buy time for reefs while global emissions are addressed."
